Subject: Serve RFC 7233 single byte ranges from HyperBEAM HTTP responses

Native immutable uploads are served directly from their message IDs. The
resolver returns the full binary message body and the HTTP layer previously
ignored the browser's Range header, producing a 200 chunked response that
cannot seek reliably. Apply one satisfiable byte range after encoding and
remove whole-message commitment headers from the derived partial response.

